Public, but NOT open source. There is no licence to use, copy, modify or distribute
this code. It is readable because the repository is public; that is not permission.

## What being public exposes, decided knowingly

  - `vendor/tokens/reference/` — the REFERENCE tier only: the 66-shade brand palette
    plus the reference spacing, radius, font, animation and transition scales, from
    `agorapulse/design`, which is itself a private repository.
  - `vendor/figma-variables.json` — the REFERENCE collection of the Agorapulse Figma
    variable export.

The inventory used to be wider on both lines, and the reduction is the point: the
`system/` and `components/` token files (263 and 508 values) and the `system` and
`component` Figma collections (130 and 69 names) were removed. The 66 reference hexes
are brand colours that appear in every shipped interface; the semantic and component
vocabulary is the internal structure of a private design system, which is a different
kind of thing to publish, and this tool never needed it — nothing outside the reference
tier is read by the engine, the wall or the fidelity harness.
  - `spec/palette.baseline.json` — five brand anchor hexes and seven family hues.
    Not the whole palette; the other 66 shades are solved from these.

The owner was shown that inventory and chose to publish. It is recorded here so
nobody has to reconstruct the decision from a commit log.

## What it does NOT carry, and why that is what made this possible

  - **No licensed typeface.** Averta is not here, in the working tree or in the
    history. This repository was started with a fresh `git init` for exactly that
    reason. The only font is Geist, OFL-1.1, from fontsource.
  - **No compiled design-system stylesheets.** `agorapulse-color-lab` vendors 1.9 MB
    of them under `public/vendor/` for its component previews. This tool has no
    preview and reads none: the palette wall paints from custom properties it writes
    itself.

That first point is the whole difference between the two repositories.
`agorapulse-color-lab` cannot be published at any price — five Averta `.otf` blobs
are live in its history, and its own NOTICE says they may not be redistributed. That
is not a .gitignore change. See `docs/decisions.md` there.
